# Security

## Trust boundary

- **Gateway** validates Bearer JWT (`JwtRelayFilter`) and **sets** `X-User-Id`, `X-User-Email`, `X-User-Roles`. Downstream services trust those headers on the private network.
- Strip / overwrite incoming `X-User-*` from the public internet. Invalid tokens proceed as **guest**, not 500.
- `/internal/**` requires `X-Internal-Key`. Gateway **does not** route `/internal/**`.
- CORS belongs **only** on the gateway. Do not enable permissive CORS on domain services.

```java
UserContext ctx = UserContextResolver.fromHeaders(request);
if (ctx.userId() == null || ctx.userId().isBlank()) {
    throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unauthorized");
}
if (!ctx.isAdmin()) {
    throw new IllegalArgumentException("Admin access required");
}
```

## Auth flows

- Passwords: BCrypt only. Never log tokens, cookies, or Stripe secrets.
- Access JWT in memory (frontend). Refresh token: **httpOnly** cookie `refreshToken`; `credentials: 'include'` on auth calls.
- Google: verify ID token (JWKS) in production; do not trust client-supplied `email`/`sub` without verification.
- Stripe webhook: no JWT. Verify signature when keys are present; persist Stripe event id uniquely so retries are idempotent.

## Frontend

- Send `Authorization: Bearer` only when an access token exists.
- Never store refresh tokens in `localStorage`. Guest cart token may live in `localStorage`.
- Gate `/admin/**` on `ADMIN` in UI **and** on the API. UI hiding is not security.

## Secrets

Keep values in `.env` (`JWT_SECRET`, `INTERNAL_API_KEY`, Stripe, Google, admin seed). Commit `.env.example` placeholders only. Never hardcode production secrets in YAML or source.
